{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d4f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a92d-72d5-7050-8a68-2291f8904dd8"},"sequence":2260,"recorded_at":1780531400004515,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"78df6718-13a7-44bd-a557-df1400b3b946","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"78df6718-13a7-44bd-a557-df1400b3b946","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"78df6718-13a7-44bd-a557-df1400b3b946"},"terminal":"completed","text":"R8 work is handed off to review (board status `to-review`, checklist 19/19, outcome artifact attached).\n\nWhat changed: the per-directory lease and all its path-identity machinery (`leaseKey`, volume-sensitivity folding, case seam) are gone, replaced by one installer-wide mutation lease — a second install/config/service/recovery for any directory is refused as installer-busy until the first settles. With no path comparison, the symlink/case/Unicode alias bypass classes cannot exist. The rev7 Unicode regression (`runner-σ`/`runner-ς`) is adopted verbatim and passes with identical inodes and a single download; three concurrency controls were converted to serialization-plus-retry proofs; three obsolete lease-key unit tests were removed. Finder-alias refusal and all identity/token/idempotency behavior are preserved.\n\nEvidence: full Core suite 158/158 green (exit 0), metadata 4/4 (exit 0), native build succeeded (exit 0), narrowing mutant M32 killed by the serialization test (exit 1, 3 issues) with same-path controls green under the mutant and pristine hash verified after revert. Candidate left uncommitted at branch tip `6b4a21d`; generator inputs untouched; production runners untouched. Full details in `TASK-260916-13diw4_outcome_v8.md`.","reason":null}}
